WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.472
From claims to practice.

2
00:00:01.752 --> 00:00:03.565
Weeks 1 and 2 were about claims.

3
00:00:03.845 --> 00:00:09.947
This week is about what labs, governments, and engineers actually do, and the evidence on whether it works.

4
00:00:10.227 --> 00:00:22.515
This lesson covers the labs’ side: the published frameworks that govern when a frontier model may be trained or deployed, the research that tries to see inside models, and the documented ways models misbehave.

5
00:00:22.795 --> 00:00:25.077
You will not write a frontier safety framework.

6
00:00:25.357 --> 00:00:33.528
You will build systems on top of these models, and every failure mode in this lesson has a small-scale version in your own agents and evals.

7
00:00:33.808 --> 00:00:40.315
Reward hacking in a lab’s RL run and an agent special-casing your test suite are the same phenomenon.

8
00:00:40.595 --> 00:00:47.635
Sycophancy in a chatbot and an LLM judge that agrees with whichever answer sounds confident are cousins.

9
00:00:47.915 --> 00:00:53.355
Reading this lesson as an engineer means asking, for each item, where it shows up in your stack.
